    {
      "source": "If you write a <code>Converter</code> whose source and target type are native types, we cannot determine whether we should consider it as a reading or a writing converter.\nRegistering the converter instance as both might lead to unwanted results.\nFor example, a <code>Converter&lt;String, Long&gt;</code> is ambiguous, although it probably does not make sense to try to convert all <code>String</code> instances into <code>Long</code> instances when writing.\nTo let you force the infrastructure to register a converter for only one way, we provide <code>@ReadingConverter</code> and <code>@WritingConverter</code> annotations to be used in the converter implementation.",
      "translation": "如果您编写了一个源类型和目标类型均为原生类型的<code>Converter</code>，我们无法确定应将其视为读取转换器还是写入转换器。  \n将转换器实例同时注册为两者可能会导致意外结果。  \n例如，<code>Converter&lt;String, Long&gt;</code>具有歧义性，尽管在写入时尝试将所有<code>String</code>实例转换为<code>Long</code>实例可能并不合理。  \n为了让您强制基础设施只为单一方向注册转换器，我们提供了<code>@ReadingConverter</code>和<code>@WritingConverter</code>注解，可在转换器实现中使用。",
      "count": 2
    },
    {
      "source": "<code>MappingCassandraConverter</code> first checks to see whether any Spring <code>Converters</code> can handle a specific class before attempting to map the object itself.\nTo \"'hijack'\" the normal mapping strategies of the <code>MappingCassandraConverter</code> (perhaps for increased performance or other custom mapping needs), you need to create an implementation of the Spring <code>Converter</code> interface and register it with the <code>MappingCassandraConverter</code>.",
      "translation": "<code>MappingCassandraConverter</code> 首先会检查是否有任何 Spring <code>Converter</code> 能够处理特定类，然后再尝试映射该对象本身。  \n若要“劫持”<code>MappingCassandraConverter</code> 的正常映射策略（例如为了提升性能或其他自定义映射需求），您需要创建一个实现 Spring <code>Converter</code> 接口的类，并将其注册到 <code>MappingCassandraConverter</code> 中。",
      "count": 2
    },
    {
      "source": "The following example of a Spring <code>Converter</code> implementation converts from a <code>String</code> to a custom <code>Email</code> value object:",
      "translation": "以下是一个 Spring <code>Converter</code> 实现的示例，它用于将 <code>String</code> 转换为自定义的 <code>Email</code> 值对象：",
      "count": 2
    },
    {
      "source": "JSR-310 Converters for conversion between <code>java.time</code>, <code>java.util.Date</code> and <code>String</code> types.",
      "translation": "用于在 `<code>java.time</code>`、`<code>java.util.Date</code>` 和 `<code>String</code>` 类型之间进行转换的 JSR-310 转换器。",
      "count": 2
    },
    {
      "source": "To have more fine-grained control over the mapping process, you can register Spring <code>Converters</code> with\n<code>CassandraConverter</code> implementations, such as <code>MappingCassandraConverter</code>.",
      "translation": "为了对映射过程进行更细粒度的控制，您可以将 Spring <code>Converters</code> 注册到 <code>CassandraConverter</code> 实现中，例如 <code>MappingCassandraConverter</code>。",
      "count": 2
    },
    {
      "source": "The following example uses a <code>Converter</code> to convert a <code>Person</code> object to a <code>java.lang.String</code>\nwith Jackson 2:",
      "translation": "以下示例使用 `<code>Converter`</code> 将 `<code>Person</code>` 对象转换为 `<code>java.lang.String</code>`，使用的是 Jackson 2：",
      "count": 2
    },
    {
      "source": "The following example uses a <code>Converter</code> that converts a <code>java.lang.String</code> into a <code>Person</code> object with Jackson 2:",
      "translation": "以下示例使用一个 `<code>Converter`</code>，通过 Jackson 2 将 `<code>java.lang.String</code>` 转换为 `<code>Person</code>` 对象：",
      "count": 2
    },
    {
      "source": "Spring Data for Apache Cassandra Java configuration provides a convenient way to register Spring <code>Converter</code> instances:\n<code>MappingCassandraConverter</code>.\nThe following configuration snippet shows how to manually register converters as well as configure <code>CustomConversions</code>:",
      "translation": "Spring Data for Apache Cassandra 的 Java 配置提供了一种便捷的方式来注册 Spring `<code>Converter`实例：`<code>MappingCassandraConverter</code>`。以下配置片段展示了如何手动注册转换器以及配置`<code>CustomConversions</code>`：",
      "count": 2
    },
    {
      "source": "Generally, we inspect the <code>Converter</code> implementations for the source and target types they convert from and to.\nDepending on whether one of those is a type the underlying data access API can handle natively, we register the converter instance as a reading or a writing converter.\nThe following examples show a writing-  and a read converter (note the difference is in the order of the qualifiers on <code>Converter</code>):",
      "translation": "通常，我们会检查 `<code>Converter`</code> 实现所转换的源类型和目标类型。根据这些类型中是否有一种是底层数据访问 API 能够原生处理的，我们将转换器实例注册为读取转换器或写入转换器。以下示例展示了一个写入转换器和一个读取转换器（请注意 `<code>Converter`</code> 上限定符的顺序差异）：",
      "count": 2
    },
    {
      "source": "Converters are subject to explicit registration as instances are not picked up from a classpath or container scan to avoid unwanted registration with a conversion service and the side effects resulting from such a registration. Converters are registered with <code>CustomConversions</code> as the central facility that allows registration and querying for registered converters based on source- and target type.",
      "translation": "转换器必须进行显式注册，因为实例不会从类路径或容器扫描中自动拾取，以避免与转换服务发生不需要的注册以及由此产生的副作用。转换器通过 <code>CustomConversions</code> 进行注册，该组件是中央设施，允许基于源类型和目标类型注册和查询已注册的转换器。",
      "count": 2
    },
    {
      "source": "<code>CustomConversions</code> ships with a pre-defined set of converter registrations:",
      "translation": "<code>CustomConversions</code> 随附一组预定义的转换器注册：",
      "count": 2
    },
    {
      "source": "You can combine converting and saving in a single process, basically using the converter to do the saving.",
      "translation": "您可以将转换与保存合并为一个流程，基本是利用转换器来完成保存操作。",
      "count": 2
    },
    {
      "source": "Similar to how you can combine saving and converting, you can also combine reading and converting.",
      "translation": "与保存和转换可以组合使用一样，读取和转换也可以组合使用。",
      "count": 2
    },
    {
